 <h2 id="how-these-projects-usually-go">How these projects usually go</h2>
 <ol><li><strong>Survey interest.</strong> Find out how many residents have or plan to buy an EV.</li><li><strong>Check the electrical capacity.</strong> A contractor looks at the building's service and where chargers could go.</li><li><strong>Start small, with room to grow.</strong> Run conduit for more spaces than you need now, and install a few chargers first.</li><li><strong>Decide how billing works.</strong> Networked chargers can bill each driver. Simpler setups put chargers on a resident's own meter.</li></ol>
