 <h2 id="outlet-or-hardwired">Outlet or hardwired?</h2>
 <ul><li><strong>Outlet (NEMA 14-50):</strong> easy to swap chargers, portable. A plug-in charger on a 50-amp circuit typically charges at up to 40 amps. Use a heavy-duty, industrial-grade receptacle; cheap ones can overheat under hours of EV charging.</li><li><strong>Hardwired:</strong> allows higher charging speeds on a bigger circuit, no plug to wear out, and it's the better fit outdoors.</li></ul>
 <h2 id="what-it-costs">What it costs</h2>
